    "skos:definition": {
      "@language": "en",
      "@value": "The APF11 controller board manufactured by Teledyne Webb for APEX floats controls the air and buoyancy pumps and interfaces with the GPS receiver, the Iridium modem, the CTD, and any additionally installed science sensors. It also includes the float's microcomputer, an internal clock, operational firmware and program and data memory, and it inputs and processes signals from a leak detector and internal temperature, pressure and humidity sensors. APF11 accommodates up to eight sensors, in addition to the conductivity, temperature and depth (CTD) sensors http://www.teledynemarine.com/news/enabling-apex-to-do-more-teledyne-webb-research-releases-apf-11-controller-and-firmware."
    },
